-- Population for the local-authority register, from CBS Census 2022.
--
-- `municipalities.official_population` was set on exactly one of 260 rows, so
-- every municipality desk printed an em dash where its resident count belongs,
-- and `municipality_civic_stats()` returned a NULL engagement score for all of
-- them - the score divides platform reach by population, so one missing column
-- silently voided a quarter of the civic index nationwide.
--
-- Provenance is per row, as the column set demands. A city is one locality and
-- takes the census figure directly. A regional council is not a locality: its
-- figure is the sum of the localities the Ministry of the Interior registry
-- assigns to it, and its source string says so rather than implying CBS
-- published a single number for it.
--
-- 245 of 259 authorities resolved (כנסת ישראל is national and has no
-- population of its own). The remaining 14 are deliberately left NULL rather
-- than guessed: some are ambiguous across the register (טייבה, טמרה and גת each
-- name more than one locality), some are industrial or dissolved councils with
-- no census locality (רמת חובב, מגדל תפן, אבו בסמה), and a wrong resident count
-- is worse than an honest em dash - it would publish a fabricated civic score.
--
-- Only NULLs are filled. A figure already set by hand is more specific than
-- this sweep and is left alone.

UPDATE public.municipalities AS m
   SET official_population   = source.population,
       population_source_name = source.source_name,
       population_source_url  = source.source_url,
       population_as_of       = DATE '2022-12-31',
       population_updated_at  = now()
  FROM (VALUES
    ('אבו גוש', 8657, 'הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה — מפקד האוכלוסין והדיור 2022', 'https://data.gov.il/dataset/2022/resource/38207cf8-afe2-48ed-a3b0-c8f70c796015'),
